Before pricing a dish, it helps to have three numbers at hand.

## The cost of each ingredient

What we pay per kilo or per unit, **after waste**: if we use 850 g out of a kilo of carrots, the real cost is higher than the receipt says.

## Cooking loss

Some preparations lose weight when cooked. That loss is paid for too.

## Servings

With the total cost of the recipe and the servings it makes, you get the cost per serving: the starting point of the price.
